2026-11-07T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2471) 'the temporal plan expresses the Challenge's precedence-only scheduling problems.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2471) 'the persona's temporal plan representation, read against four candidate problem sets.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2471) 'After the planning puzzles, can the same temporal plan express a problem that needs only precedence and durations, with no resources at all?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2471) 'Four problem families on the Challenge's list look like a fit by name alone: project-planning (2012, 2015), road_construction (2014, 2017), ship-schedule (2011, 2012, 2014) and train-scheduling (2024). None of their models has been read yet, so fit is a guess today. The temporal plan already carries start, end and duration per step, release times and deadlines, and a critical-path total, but it has no resources, so any model with a cumulative constraint is out of reach before a single model is read.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2471) 'Read one family's model in full and classify it: expressible on the temporal plan as is, or out of reach because it needs a resource, an all-different, a cumulative or a packing constraint the plan does not carry.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2471) 'MiniZinc Challenge: precedence-scheduling problems on the temporal plan
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2471) 'Read each of the four candidate families' models, starting with the smallest, and classify each as expressible or out of reach by the same rule the planning puzzles used. For a family that is expressible, climb from its smallest instance, validate every plan against MiniZinc itself, and accept only a plan that is both valid and optimal. A family that needs a resource, an all-different, a cumulative or a packing constraint is set aside rather than forced onto a plan that cannot carry it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2471) '- RFD66606-2339, where a persona answers from a goal-task network and exports a plan.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2471  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2471) '- RFD66606-2292, the organization's own RECTGTN (Lean goal-task network) domain that renders this register.
